-- ethanol, the smallest compound whose count depends on the medium other than glycine, and the one
-- whose spectrum every student learns. Atoms: 0 the methyl carbon with hydrogens 1 to 3, 4 the methylene
-- carbon with hydrogens 5 and 6, 7 the oxygen with hydrogen 8. The methylene hydrogens are enantiotopic:
-- substituting one makes that carbon a stereocentre and the two products are mirror images. So an
-- achiral solvent identifies them and a chiral solvent does not, and the familiar triplet and quartet
-- are a fact about ethanol in an achiral solvent rather than about ethanol.
num-eth-obs : List Nat
num-eth-obs = cons 1 (cons 2 (cons 3 (cons 5 (cons 6 nil))))
